{"orgCode":"0950","name":"State Treasurer","agencyCode":"0010","agencyName":"Legislative, Judicial, and Executive","description":"The State Treasurer, a constitutionally established office, provides banking services for state government with goals to minimize interest and service costs and to maximize yield on investments. The Treasurer is responsible for the custody of all monies and securities belonging to or held in trust by the state; investment of temporarily idle state monies; administration of the sale of state bonds, their redemption and interest payments; and payment of warrants or checks drawn by the State Controller and other state agencies.","totals":{"amounts":{"py":11886,"cy":15387,"by":16236},"positions":{"py":216.4,"cy":243.4,"by":243.4},"excluded":{"reimbursement":{"py":23455,"cy":26877,"by":27008},"nongovernmental":{"py":6727,"cy":7557,"by":7140}}},"programs":{"id":"exp/0010/0950","kind":"department","name":"State Treasurer","code":"0950","amounts":{"py":11886,"cy":15387,"by":16236},"positions":{"py":216.4,"cy":243.4,"by":243.4},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":11886,"cy":15387,"by":16236}},"children":[{"id":"exp/0010/0950/0740","kind":"program","name":"State Treasurer's Office","code":"0740","amounts":{"py":11886,"cy":15387,"by":16236},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":11886,"cy":15387,"by":16236}},"extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":42068,"cy":49821,"by":50384}}},"children":[{"id":"exp/0010/0950/0740010","kind":"subprogram","name":"Investment Services","code":"0740010","amounts":{"py":450,"cy":865,"by":913},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":450,"cy":865,"by":913}},"positions":{"py":19,"cy":19,"by":19},"description":"0740010 - INVESTMENT SERVICES\n\nThe Investment Division is responsible for investment of state monies through the Pooled Money Investment Account (PMIA), from the date of receipt through the date of redemption. During the 2024-25 fiscal year, this Division handled 13,358 security investment transactions totaling $659.3 billion. Investments through the PMIA accounted for 12,488 of these transactions totaling $620.8 billion; time deposits accounted for 739 transactions totaling $25.8 billion. The remaining $12.7 billion is invested on behalf of the state's special funds, such as those associated with the California Housing Finance Agency, the Department of Fish and Wildlife, the state's retirement system, etc. The Division also administers the Local Agency Investment Fund (LAIF), a voluntary investment program created to offer California local agencies greater access to the financial markets through the PMIB program. In the 2024-25 fiscal year, 2,334 local agencies participated in LAIF, with deposits averaging $21.6 billion for the fiscal year.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":5806,"cy":5591,"by":6134}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/0010/0950/0740010/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":450,"cy":865,"by":913},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":450,"cy":865,"by":913}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":450,"cy":865,"by":913}}}}],"excludedChildren":[{"id":"exp/0010/0950/0740010/f0995","kind":"fund","name":"Reimbursements","code":"0995","amounts":{"py":4132,"cy":3972,"by":4514},"byFundType":{"reimbursement":{"py":4132,"cy":3972,"by":4514}},"extra":{"fundType":"reimbursement","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":4132,"cy":3972,"by":4514}}}},{"id":"exp/0010/0950/0740010/f9740","kind":"fund","name":"Central Service Cost Recovery Fund","code":"9740","amounts":{"py":1224,"cy":754,"by":707},"byFundType":{"nongovernmental":{"py":1224,"cy":754,"by":707}},"extra":{"fundType":"nongovernmental","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":1224,"cy":754,"by":707}}}}],"excluded":{"reimbursement":{"py":4132,"cy":3972,"by":4514},"nongovernmental":{"py":1224,"cy":754,"by":707}}},{"id":"exp/0010/0950/0740019","kind":"subprogram","name":"Centralized Treasury & Securities Management","code":"0740019","amounts":{"py":4623,"cy":6217,"by":6448},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":4623,"cy":6217,"by":6448}},"positions":{"py":49.7,"cy":59.5,"by":59.5},"description":"0740019 - CENTRALIZED TREASURY AND SECURITIES MANAGEMENT\n\nIn 1949, the California Legislature amended Government Code Section 16305 to create the Centralized Treasury System (CTS) thereby requiring agencies of the State to deposit their money in trust with the Treasurer. The legislation also requires the Treasurer to safeguard the money and make safe and prudent investments. In 1955, the Legislature created the PMIB, giving the PMIB the responsibility to designate the amount of money available for the investment in securities, bank deposits, and loans to the General Fund.\n\nThe Centralized Treasury and Securities Management Division (CTSMD) oversees all banking aspects of the CTS. The goal of the CTSMD is to maximize the earning of interest consistent with safe and prudent treasury management, and to ensure that the depository banks provide the state with proper and adequate security for the deposit of state monies. The Treasurer maintains demand bank accounts with seven banks for the purpose of providing necessary statewide depository coverage for the remittance of funds collected by the various state agencies.\n\nThe CTSMD 1) monitors the cash flow of all state funds, forecasts cash balances, revenue, expenditures, and the amounts available for daily investments, 2) ensures accurate and timely agency deposits, 3) administers and executes the wire transfer of funds, 4) reconciles state accounts with depository banks, 5) redeems all state items submitted by presenting banks for payment, 6) executes the clearance and income collection for state investments (excluding PERS and STRS) and securities pledged to the state, 7) fulfills the clearance and settlement of securities pledged to the state as collateral for the time, demand, and other state agency programs, and 8) is responsible for the safekeeping of securities and other personal property owned by or pledged to the state.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":14417,"cy":18229,"by":18247}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/0010/0950/0740019/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":4623,"cy":6217,"by":6448},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":4623,"cy":6217,"by":6448}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":4623,"cy":6217,"by":6448}}}}],"excludedChildren":[{"id":"exp/0010/0950/0740019/f0995","kind":"fund","name":"Reimbursements","code":"0995","amounts":{"py":7387,"cy":8339,"by":8347},"byFundType":{"reimbursement":{"py":7387,"cy":8339,"by":8347}},"extra":{"fundType":"reimbursement","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":7387,"cy":8339,"by":8347}}}},{"id":"exp/0010/0950/0740019/f9740","kind":"fund","name":"Central Service Cost Recovery Fund","code":"9740","amounts":{"py":2407,"cy":3673,"by":3452},"byFundType":{"nongovernmental":{"py":2407,"cy":3673,"by":3452}},"extra":{"fundType":"nongovernmental","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":2407,"cy":3673,"by":3452}}}}],"excluded":{"reimbursement":{"py":7387,"cy":8339,"by":8347},"nongovernmental":{"py":2407,"cy":3673,"by":3452}}},{"id":"exp/0010/0950/0740028","kind":"subprogram","name":"Public Finance","code":"0740028","amounts":{"py":4750,"cy":4216,"by":4387},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":4750,"cy":4216,"by":4387}},"positions":{"py":54.6,"cy":60,"by":60},"description":"0740028 - PUBLIC FINANCE\n\nThe Public Finance Division is responsible for selling State of California general obligation bonds, commercial paper notes, revenue anticipation notes, lease revenue bonds, revenue bonds, and any other indebtedness for all state agencies. The Division provides debt administration services for most state bonds and is responsible for disseminating information to bondholders through the Investor Relations Program.\n\nThe Division also assures compliance with federal tax laws applicable to certain state debt so there is no adverse consequences to bondholders or increased borrowing costs to the state. The post-issuance tax compliance includes monitoring the use of bond proceeds, managing rebate and yield restriction compliance, coordinating necessary financial disclosure, and ensuring proper record keeping.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":15816,"cy":16004,"by":16016}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/0010/0950/0740028/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":4750,"cy":4216,"by":4387},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":4750,"cy":4216,"by":4387}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":4750,"cy":4216,"by":4387}}}}],"excludedChildren":[{"id":"exp/0010/0950/0740028/f0995","kind":"fund","name":"Reimbursements","code":"0995","amounts":{"py":7970,"cy":9184,"by":9190},"byFundType":{"reimbursement":{"py":7970,"cy":9184,"by":9190}},"extra":{"fundType":"reimbursement","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":7970,"cy":9184,"by":9190}}}},{"id":"exp/0010/0950/0740028/f9740","kind":"fund","name":"Central Service Cost Recovery Fund","code":"9740","amounts":{"py":3096,"cy":2604,"by":2439},"byFundType":{"nongovernmental":{"py":3096,"cy":2604,"by":2439}},"extra":{"fundType":"nongovernmental","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":3096,"cy":2604,"by":2439}}}}],"excluded":{"reimbursement":{"py":7970,"cy":9184,"by":9190},"nongovernmental":{"py":3096,"cy":2604,"by":2439}}},{"id":"exp/0010/0950/0740035","kind":"subprogram","name":"Administration","code":"0740035","amounts":{"py":2063,"cy":4089,"by":4488},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":2063,"cy":4089,"by":4488}},"positions":{"py":93.1,"cy":104.9,"by":104.9},"description":"0740035 - ADMINISTRATION AND INFORMATION SERVICES\n\r\nThe Administration Division, Executive Office, and the Information Services Division provide executive direction and support services to programs in the State Treasurer's Office. Services include budgeting, personnel, accounting, information systems, business services, technical support, and production operations.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":6029,"cy":9997,"by":9987}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/0010/0950/0740035/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":2063,"cy":4089,"by":4488},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":2063,"cy":4089,"by":4488}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":2063,"cy":4089,"by":4488}}}}],"excludedChildren":[{"id":"exp/0010/0950/0740035/f0995","kind":"fund","name":"Reimbursements","code":"0995","amounts":{"py":3966,"cy":5382,"by":4957},"byFundType":{"reimbursement":{"py":3966,"cy":5382,"by":4957}},"extra":{"fundType":"reimbursement","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":3966,"cy":5382,"by":4957}}}},{"id":"exp/0010/0950/0740035/f9740","kind":"fund","name":"Central Service Cost Recovery Fund","code":"9740","amounts":{"py":0,"cy":526,"by":542},"byFundType":{"nongovernmental":{"py":0,"cy":526,"by":542}},"extra":{"fundType":"nongovernmental","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":0,"cy":526,"by":542}}}}],"excluded":{"reimbursement":{"py":3966,"cy":5382,"by":4957},"nongovernmental":{"py":0,"cy":526,"by":542}}}],"excluded":{"reimbursement":{"py":23455,"cy":26877,"by":27008},"nongovernmental":{"py":6727,"cy":7557,"by":7140}}}],"sources":[{"label":"ebudget.ca.gov API: orgProgram/0950","url":"https://ebudget.ca.gov/api/budget/e/2026-27/orgProgram/0950"},{"label":"Detailed Expenditures by Program (PDF)","url":"https://ebudget.ca.gov/2026-27/pdf/Enacted/GovernorsBudget/0010/0950.pdf"}],"extra":{"legalCitations":"DEPARTMENT AUTHORITY\n\nCalifornia Constitution Article XVI, Sections 1.5 and 7; and Government Code Sections 5700-5703, 12302-12333, 16300, 16650-16857."},"excluded":{"reimbursement":{"py":23455,"cy":26877,"by":27008},"nongovernmental":{"py":6727,"cy":7557,"by":71